# This file gates nothing today, and that is a recorded decision rather than an
# oversight. The ruleset at .github/rulesets/protect-main.json sets
# required_approving_review_count to 0 and require_code_owner_review to false,
# and GitHub never requests a review from a pull request's own author, so on a
# one-person repository an owner entry can only ever name the person who opened
# the pull request. GITHUB section 5 says when that changes: required approvals
# go from 0 to 1 as soon as a second person joins, and section 9 says where the
# number is set, which is the ruleset file named above and not this one. Until
# then the owner is stated so that the answer is already written down, and
# tests/unit/repository-hygiene.test.ts fails if either ruleset value starts
# asking for a review while this comment still says neither does.
* @Elia-Youssef
